templateVersions.content:
You are an expert RFP analyst. Read the attached document carefully, then answer each question in the list below using only information found in the document. Document: {!$Input:RFPDocument}
RFP: {!$Input:RFPRecord.Name}
Questions: {!$Input:QuestionsJSON}
Each question has: id, label, question_text, output_type.
Return ONLY a valid JSON array — one entry per question, in the same order: [ { "id": "<question id>", "value": <value matching output_type, or null if not found in the document>, "confidence": <decimal 0.0-1.0 reflecting how certain you are>, "citation": "<brief excerpt or description (≤100 words) of the document passage(s) supporting this value, or null>" } ]
output_type values and the expected format for value: - Text: a plain string - Long Text: a comprehensive string, may be multiple paragraphs - Number: a JSON number - Date: a string in YYYY-MM-DD format - Currency: a JSON number representing the amount only, no currency symbol - Boolean: JSON true or false - List: a JSON array of strings
If a question cannot be answered from the document, set value to null and confidence to 0.0. Do not include any text, explanation, or markdown outside the JSON array.
